{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfWAj4iwpDMiVxDxBxxHR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The report is written to `/app/report.json` naming **H-4** as the change to roll back, with an external-suite gain interval of **2.40 to 2.85 points**.\n\n**What the investigation found**\n\n- **Most of the dashboard drop was a harness artifact.** Scoring release under the old harness gave about 56.3, and scoring previous under the new harness gave about 54.7. The harness change alone moves scores by roughly 4 points, and single-revert harness scans pinned that to H-1 and H-2. Those two changes do not affect the external suite, so rolling either back would buy customers nothing.\n- **The real model regression is H-4.** Retraining with each change rolled back individually and scoring under a fixed harness gave one clear standout. The H-4 rollback scored about 2.6 points above release, while H-3 gained under 1 point and H-1, H-2, and H-5 gained nothing or slightly regressed.\n- **The external suite confirmed it.** Eight external units each on release and on the H-4 rollback checkpoint gave a difference of 2.62 points with a standard error of about 0.13. The in-house fixed-harness difference of 2.63 agrees almost exactly, and combining the two estimates gives 2.63 with a standard error near 0.09.\n\n**Interval choice**\n\nThe interval is centered on the pooled estimate at the maximum allowed width of 0.45, which covers roughly 2.6 standard errors on each side. All 120 credits were spent, with the final credit used to confirm that the H-4 rollback under the old harness lands at 58.8, matching the pre-release dashboard number."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":32610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":528,"service_tier":"standard"